// Go workspace for this repository.
//
// There are two modules and they are not peers:
//
//	sync/         the generator. Real code, built and vetted here.
//	sandbox/go/   a go.mod *template*, copied over gen/go in CI so the
//	              generated protobuf Go can be compiled. It holds no
//	              packages of its own.
//
// Only the generator is a workspace member. The template is deliberately
// left out: adding it would put a module in the workspace that has nothing
// to build, and the tree it describes -- gen/go -- does not exist until
// `buf generate` has run.
//
// That omission has a consequence worth knowing. Once a go.work exists at the
// repository root, a `go build` run *inside* gen/go resolves this workspace
// and fails, because gen/go is not a member. CI and the justfile therefore
// set GOWORK=off for that build; see .github/workflows/generate.yml.
go 1.24

use ./sync
